Except, of course, that it renders artifact wishing forbidden until you
more or less no longer need to in the first place.  It would require
some very delicate balancing to make sure you still leave that sort of
thing open.

And isn't one of the great sources of appeal of this game the fountain
wish?  We see tons of dead players trying for it all the time on NAO...
why would you want to cripple their hopes by saying "Yeah, even though
you could take risks and kill many characters to get one, you can't wish
for anything GOOD.."

> Bones files containing quest artifacts are far and wide and most of all
> normally not very shallow.

They aren't exactly so far and wide as you think, on a public server...
nor are they particularly deep.  They'll almost all be before Gehennom,
for example, since nobody dies there.

The Orb of Fate is a particularly common pickup, as is the Eye of
Tapioca.  Why?  Because those are two of the easy quests, so it's
possible to get the artifact while still crunchy enough to die pre-castle.

